---
import ContentPage from '../../components/ContentPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'When should I reorganize furniture?', answer: 'Review the arrangement when the dining area becomes difficult to read or when furniture no longer fits the restaurant plan.' },
  { question: 'Should I change the whole dining area at once?', answer: 'Small changes are easier to evaluate. Adjust one section, follow the normal service route, and continue only when the new arrangement remains clear.' },
  { question: 'Where can I browse table entries?', answer: 'Use the Tables directory for the individual table pages currently available in the Wiki.' },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title="Karinderya Furniture Management Guide"
  description="Learn how to review, rearrange, and manage existing furniture while planning a clear Karinderya restaurant layout."
  kicker="Furniture management guide"
  intro="Manage existing furniture around dining-area organization and restaurant layout."
  parent={{ label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }}
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.furnitureHero}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Furniture Hub', href: '/furniture/', description: 'Browse Furniture categories and planning guidance.' },
    { label: 'Tables', href: '/furniture/tables/', description: 'Open the Tables directory and individual entries.' },
    { label: 'Chairs', href: '/furniture/chairs/', description: 'Review Chairs as part of the dining area.' },
    { label: 'Restaurant Layout Guide', href: '/guides/restaurant-layout/', description: 'Plan dining, kitchen, and movement areas.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>Furniture management is the process of reviewing the current dining area and deciding how existing pieces fit into the restaurant plan. Focus on organization, movement, and clear customer spaces rather than treating furniture as an isolated list of items.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Tables and Chairs help define the dining area. As the restaurant layout changes, furniture may need to be moved, replaced, or reconsidered through the controls currently available in the game. The Furniture Hub provides category information, while this guide focuses on planning decisions.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
  <p>Use the current furniture or editing interface to select an item and review the actions shown on screen. Before changing the arrangement, identify the space you want to improve and consider how the surrounding dining and movement areas will be affected.</p>

  <h2 id="furniture-management-process">Furniture Management Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Review the current dining area and identify the section that needs attention.</li>
    <li>Open the furniture controls available in the current game.</li>
    <li>Select the relevant Table, Chair, or other furniture item.</li>
    <li>Read the available actions before confirming a change.</li>
    <li>Adjust the surrounding space so customer and movement areas remain clear.</li>
    <li>Follow a normal service route and refine the arrangement if needed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="layout-planning">Layout Planning</h2>
  <p>Keep dining furniture grouped as a recognizable customer area. Coordinate it with the kitchen and serving route, and use the <a href="/guides/restaurant-layout/">Restaurant Layout Guide</a> when a change affects more than one section of the restaurant.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Change one part of the dining area at a time.</li>
    <li>Keep furniture controls and important interactions easy to identify.</li>
    <li>Use the Tables and Chairs directories when reviewing category information.</li>
    <li>Plan furniture alongside the wider restaurant layout.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Changing several dining-area sections before reviewing the result.</li>
    <li>Focusing on appearance while movement routes become unclear.</li>
    <li>Managing an item without checking the actions shown by the current interface.</li>
    <li>Treating furniture separately from kitchen and serving organization.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</ContentPage>
